# Secrets. Credentials live in Supabase Vault; these are only local convenience.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/

# Local state
eval/results/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The Claude Code agent's local cursor file lives in the user's home directory,
# not here, but ignore any stray copy.
.content-system-state.json

# Generated by cc-agent/install.mjs — a shim that loads .env before the agent.
cc-agent/run-scheduled.mjs

# Evaluation harness credentials. See eval/.env.example.
eval/.env

# Deploy artefact, rebuilt by the host. Never committed.
app/desk-deploy.zip

# Josh's call recordings (docs/from-josh/README.md, "Two cautions before sending").
# Redacted, but he flagged that the 31 August call keeps clinical vertical language and anyone in
# that market could infer the client. Git history is permanent and this repository is the handover
# vehicle, so they stay out of it until he decides whether that is acceptable. They are on disk and
# in his Drive either way; nothing is lost by waiting for his answer.
docs/from-josh/transcripts/

# HTTP MCP tokens (mcp-server/mint-http-tokens.mjs). Secrets, never committed.
mcp-server/.http-tokens

# Supabase CLI scratch — project ref and service versions, rewritten on every command.
supabase/.temp/

# Exported session transcripts. They contain whatever was pasted into the session, which has
# included API keys more than once.
20*-this-session-is-being-continued-*.txt

# Personal, per-machine Claude Code settings. settings.json is the shared one.
# This file was tracked until 14 Oct 2026 and shipped a pre-approved allow-list —
# execute_sql and a functions deploy against the live project — to anyone who cloned.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ─── The 21 October clear-out ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Untracked rather than deleted, so the copies stay on our disk and nothing is lost. They leave the
# repository because the repository is what Josh clones, and none of this is his.
#
# NOTE ON WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO: every one of these files is still in the pushed history of a PUBLIC
# repository. Untracking stops them reaching a fresh clone; it does not unpublish them. Only making
# the repo private changes that, and on 21 October the decision was to leave it public for now.

# Two scrapes of the reference writers, 182 posts in full text. Superseded by the 1,900 in Postgres,
# and other people's writing does not belong in a public repo under clause 8.3.
data/josh/sentinels/scrape-2026-10-05.json
data/josh/sentinels/scrape-2026-10-09.json

# Our working notes. Written to think with, never for Josh.
docs/00-spec-understanding.md
docs/05-walkthrough.md
docs/06-roadmap.md
docs/TODO.md
docs/status-2026-10-05.md
docs/2026-10-14-call-tracker.md
docs/build-report.html
docs/build-status.html
docs/Josh fryszer-report.pdf

# Superseded by the dated SEND- files beside it. An undated "send this" is the one a future session
# picks up by mistake.
docs/to-josh/SEND-THIS.md

# The 26 October retrospective. Internal, candid, and about his business before anyone else's: it
# names the client, says what we got wrong, and carries the "0 of 62 approved" figure. The
# repository is public and its history is permanent, so this one stays on our disk — same reasoning
# as the 21 October clear-out above.
docs/retrospective-2026-10-26.md

# Written by scripts/stamp-build.mjs before a deploy. Never committed: a stamp in git is wrong
# the moment the next commit lands, and a confidently wrong version is worse than an honest one.
mcp-server/build.json
